meta {
  name: Get Access Token - Invalid Credentials
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{auth_base_url}}/auth/api/get-token
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "api_key": "{{process.env.PLYTIX_API_KEY}}",
    "api_password": "intentionally-wrong-password"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
  res.body.error.msg: isString
}

docs {
  Trigger case: confirms the documented 401 path, using the real api_key
  with a deliberately wrong password. Confirmed live 2026-08-31.

  ## Confirmed behavior (differs from the v1 Postman collection's docs)
  Documented 401 body: `{ "msg": "Bad api_key or api_password" }`

  Actual live body:
  ```json
  {
    "error": {
      "msg": "Bad api_key or api_password: Credentials not valid",
      "errors": [ { "field": "http_status_code", "msg": 401 } ]
    }
  }
  ```
  The error is nested one level deeper (`error.msg`, not top-level `msg`),
  carries an extended message, and includes an `errors` array whose single
  entry oddly reports the field name as `"http_status_code"` rather than
  `api_key`/`api_password`. Any doc page or client code written against
  the collection's documented shape will break on this response.
}
